From 07e3fbfcd034ef8c3adfda306df26ecb435bbf5f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brendan King <Brendan.King@imgtec.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Mar 2022 19:08:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 01/71] Add PVR Gallium driver

The driver is essentially a Gallium frontend for the proprietary
Imagination Technologies driver. It makes use of the Gallium DRI
infrastructure, but little else.

Some query renderer driver extension infrastructure has been
restored, as the PVR driver doesn't support the Gallium pipe
screen get_param function.

A DRI Driver Compatibility extension function has been implemented,
to check the compatibility of the render and display GPUs. This
relies on another IMG patch, "dri2: add a driver compatibility check
extension".

For DRI Driver API version 2, the is_pixmap parameter of the
createBuffer entry point may be set true if the drawable is a
pixmap. This relies on two other IMG patches, "gallium: add support
for image driver createNewDrawableType", and "loader/dri3: indicate
to driver when drawable is a pixmap".

Add support for queryCompatibleRenderOnlyDeviceFd. This also requires
changes to the PVR DRI Support library within the IMG Rogue DDK.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [oe specific]

